[ti:Seeing Hands]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.44]Lesson 4 | 第4课
[00:02.94]Seeing hands | 能“看”的手
[00:09.61]How did Vera disover she had this gift of second sight? | 薇拉是如何发现自己有这种透视的特异功能的？
[00:16.12]Several cases have been reported in Russia recently of people who can read and detect colours with their fingers, and even see through solid doors and walls. | 俄罗斯最近报道了几个事例，有人能用手指阅读和辨认颜色，甚至能看穿坚实的门和墙。
[00:27.32]One case concerns an 11-year-old schoolgirl Vera Petrova, | 其中一个事例说的是一个名叫薇拉·彼得罗娃的11岁女学生，
[00:32.15]who has normal vision but who can also perceive things with different parts of her skin, and through solid walls. | 她视力正常，但还能用身体其他部位的皮肤感知事物，甚至能看穿坚实的墙壁。
[00:40.70]This ability was first noticed by her father. | 这种能力最先是被她父亲发现的。
[00:44.14]One day she came into his office and happened to put her hands on the door of a locked safe. | 一天，她走进父亲的办公室，碰巧把手放在一个上了锁的保险柜的门上。
[00:50.44]Suddenly she asked her father why he kept so many old newspapers locked away there, | 她突然问父亲，为什么把这么多旧报纸锁在里面，
[00:56.18]and even described the way they were done up in bundles. | 甚至还描述了这些报纸捆扎成捆的样子。
[01:00.32]Vera's curious talent was brought to the notice of a scientific research institute in the town of Ulyanovsk, near where she lives, | 薇拉的奇特才能引起了离她家不远的乌里扬诺夫斯克城一家科学研究所的注意，
[01:09.76]and in April she was given a series of tests by a special commission of the Ministry of Health of the Russian Federal Republic. | 4月，俄罗斯联邦卫生部的一个特别委员会对她进行了一系列测试。
[01:19.54]During these tests she was able to read a newspaper through an opaque screen and, stranger still, | 在这些测试中，她能隔着一块不透明的屏板阅读报纸，更为奇怪的是，
[01:25.45]by moving her elbow over a child's game of Lotto she was able to describe the figures and colours printed on it; | 她把胳膊肘放在儿童玩的“罗托”纸牌上，就能描述印在纸牌上的数字和颜色；
[01:32.91]and, in another instance, wearing stockings and slippers, | 在另一个实例中，她穿着长筒袜和拖鞋，
[01:36.72]to make out with her foot the outlines and colours of a picture hidden under a carpet. | 能用脚识别出藏在地毯下面的一幅画的轮廓和颜色。
[01:42.69]Other experiments showed that her knees and shoulders had a similar sensitivity. | 其他实验表明，她的膝盖和双肩也有类似的感知能力。
[01:48.26]During all these tests Vera was blindfold; and indeed, except when blindfold she lacked the ability to perceive things with her skin. | 在所有这些测试中，薇拉的双眼都是蒙着的；而且说也奇怪，只要不蒙上眼睛，她就不具备用皮肤感知事物的能力。
[01:56.86]It was also found that although she could perceive things with her fingers this ability ceased the moment her hands were wet. | 人们还发现，尽管她能用手指感知事物，但她的手一弄湿，这种能力便立即消失。
